// The lambda parameter of the map() below is deliberately called x: the query that reads termTypes
// also uses x for its own lambda parameter. The mapping expression is routed while the query's x is
// still in scope, and the inner x - which iterates a JSON array and so has no mapping set to bind
// to - must resolve to the array element, not to the query's x.
###Mapping
Mapping demo::mct::mapping::M2MMapping
(
  *demo::mct::model::Document: Pure
  {
    ~src demo::mct::source::DocumentRow
    id: $src.id,
    version: $src.version,
    ref: $src.content.ref,
    termTypes: $src.content.terms->map(x | $x->toOne()->typeName())
  }
)
